# LocalAI Studio — repository .gitignore
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file blocks runtime, machine-local, and personal data from being
# committed by accident. Even though the publish workflow in
# tools/maintenance/update_repo.bat only copies files explicitly listed in
# manifest.txt, this is a defense-in-depth backstop if anything is added
# to the repo by other means (git add, IDE, manual copy, etc.).

# ── Private SKU / configuration data ────────────────────────────────────────
# Root-level only ('/' anchor): we INTENTIONALLY ship samples/skus.json as
# a reference example. A bare 'skus.json' here would also match
# samples/skus.json and silently exclude it.
/skus.json
/w365_skus.json
config.json
python_path.bat
comfyui_path.bat

# ── Runtime logs and per-run output ─────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
localai.log
setup.log
comfyui.log
benchmark_results/
toolbox_outputs/
Scratchpad/
*.cache/
vm_sku_detection_*.txt
localai_benchmark_candidates.json

# ── Backups and archives (never shipped to GitHub) ──────────────────────────
Archive/
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.bak2
*.bak3
pre-edit-backup-*/
pre-publish-backup-*/
pre-refimg-*/

# ── Release artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LocalAI_v*.zip
LocalAI-portable*.zip
*_patch.zip

# ── Internal AI-agent guidance and coordination state ───────────────────────
# These files describe the project to local AI agents (Claude, GPT, etc.)
# and contain private workflow notes. They are intentionally not part of
# the public repository.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.coordination/
coord.bat

# ── Bundled third-party runtimes (installed separately by setup) ────────────
ComfyUI/
Ollama/

# ── Python build / cache artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.whl

# ── IDE / editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── OS junk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# ── Personal-data leak guards ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any path containing personal identifiers should never be committed.
# These patterns are intentionally aggressive — adjust only if a legitimate
# file is being blocked.
*ronmart*
*CPC-ronma*
*OneDrive*

# ── Author-only docs that must never ship ───────────────────────────────────
docs/model-summary.html
docs/localai-docs-extension.js

# ── Maintainer-only publish tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────
# tools/maintenance/ holds the scripts that produce this repository from the
# maintainer's working copy (update_repo.bat, scrub_grep.ps1, manifest.txt,
# verify_manifest.ps1, push_to_github.bat). They are useful locally for the
# publish workflow but are not intended for public consumption — external
# users don't run them and shouldn't need to read them. Kept locally in
# C:\repos\LocalAI\tools\maintenance\ so the maintainer can run them; this
# .gitignore ensures they never end up on GitHub.
tools/maintenance/

# ---- Mac shell launchers (public repo is Windows-only) ------------------
# All .sh launchers (setup.sh, run.sh, etc.) are intentionally kept out of
# the public repo. The manifest does not list them and scrub_grep.ps1 has
# them in the Forbidden list. This *.sh ignore is a third layer — if any
# .sh file is accidentally added via git add ., it stays untracked.
*.sh

